THIRD-PARTY CONTENT ATTRIBUTIONS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

1) Rail network – Queensland
   Source: Queensland Spatial Catalogue
   URL: https://qldspatial.information.qld.gov.au/catalogue/custom/search.page?q=%22Rail%20network%20-%20Queensland%22
   Publisher: Queensland Government
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Used for: network topology for simulation input files
   Date accessed: 25/03/2025
   Modifications: Subset extraction, filtering and transformation to DesRail format, augmented with hypothetical network operations data
   Attribution statement:
   “Rail network – Queensland, Queensland Government, CC BY 4.0. Source: Queensland Spatial Catalogue.”

2) Translink General Transit Feed Specification (GTFS)
   Source: Queensland Government Open Data Portal
   URL: https://www.data.qld.gov.au/dataset/general-transit-feed-specification-gtfs-translink
   Endpoint: https://gtfsrt.api.translink.com.au/GTFS/SEQ_GTFS.zip
   Publisher: Transport and Main Roads (TransLink), Queensland Government
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Used for: the booked timetable behind the inner Brisbane scenarios — service list, calling
           patterns, booked arrival and departure times, and scheduled platforms
   Date accessed: 08/09/2026, snapshotted alongside the realtime capture below
   Modifications: subset to rail trips traversing the inner Brisbane core; conversion to DesRail
           spawner and task records; derivation of inter-station running times and of terminal
           assignments through a hand-built stop-to-terminal platform map
   Attribution statement:
   “Translink General Transit Feed Specification (GTFS), Transport and Main Roads, CC BY 4.0.
    Source: Queensland Government Open Data Portal.”

3) Translink real-time data
   Source: Queensland Government Open Data Portal
   URL: https://www.data.qld.gov.au/dataset/translink-real-time-data
   Endpoint: https://gtfsrt.api.translink.com.au/api/realtime/SEQ/{TripUpdates,VehiclePositions}/Rail
   Publisher: Transport and Main Roads (TransLink), Queensland Government
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Used for: observed arrival and departure times, dwell, and the platform each service actually
           used; the basis for the out-of-sample validation, for the recorded injection scenarios,
           and for the platform-reassignment comparison
   Date accessed: captured by repeated polling from 08/09/2026 to 10/09/2026 (UTC)
   Modifications: polled at intervals and distilled to the last value published for each
           (trip, stop) after the vehicle passed, since the feed publishes predictions and flags
           nothing as observed; anchored per trip to local midnight; reduced to stop_events.csv
           and platform_calls.csv
   Attribution statement:
   “Translink real-time data, Transport and Main Roads, CC BY 4.0.
    Source: Queensland Government Open Data Portal.”

   Note: TransLink keeps no historical archive and replaces both feeds in place, so the raw
   capture is published with the derived files; it cannot be obtained again.


